# Caddy reverse proxy: terminates HTTPS (auto Let's Encrypt) and forwards to n8n
# over the internal Docker network. n8n itself publishes no host port, so this is
# the ONLY public entrypoint. Replace n8n.example.com with your real subdomain
# (its DNS A record must point at this box before `docker compose up`).
#
# OPTIONAL hardening — restrict who can even reach the editor. Uncomment to allow
# only your office/VPN IPs (the editor is a high-value target; the fewer who can
# reach the login, the better). Leave commented to rely on the owner login alone.
#
#   @blocked not remote_ip 203.0.113.10 203.0.113.11
#   respond @blocked 403

n8n.example.com {
    reverse_proxy n8n:5678
}
